#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
ERC 2026 - final waypoint-based navigator, built from real measured
coordinates (not spec estimates).

Flow:
  1. Rotate in place from the START pose (proven CW search + OCR) until
     the target shelf digit is found and centered
  2. Identify WHICH of the 5 physical slots this is, by comparing the
     centered heading against the 5 pre-computed reference bearings
     (computed from your measured slot positions)
  3. Drive to that slot's exact measured (x, y, yaw) using closed-loop
     odometry (rotate-to-face -> drive straight, with overshoot-safe
     signed distance -> final rotate to match the measured approach yaw)
  4. Sweep head tilts for the target book colour, publish its 3D point
     for manipulation_node to grasp
  5. Drive back to the measured BIN/drop-off pose
  (Step 6, actually triggering the place-in-bin sequence, needs one more
  small addition to manipulation_node.py - a subscribed "bin point" topic
  - not yet wired in this version. Flagging this clearly rather than
  guessing at manipulation_node's interface.)
"""
